ain his son as  both the forces of Frieza and earth set  themselves on a collision course it's  now only a matter of time before all  three main characters clash for the  first time fated for this meeting this  fight goes on for almost 40 minutes and  it's not only the best Dragon Ball has  ever looked but it's one of the most  visually impressive sequences of  animation I have ever seen the  ridiculous amount of effort that went  into this film if it wasn't clear before  it most certainly should be now and  while I'm sure many of you will be  familiar with this fight I'm gonna try  to break it down and maybe point out a  few things here and there that you might  have missed the fight itself can be  divided into three sections with each  section serving a particular purpose  within the story  Broly versus vegeta to kick things off  Broly versus goku that takes up the  middle section and finally Gogeta vs.  Broly to end everything and it just so  happens that each of these three  sections focuses on the unique strengths  of each individual fight for instance a  vegeta fight is most entertaining when  he is styling on his opponent and in  control of  action we don't often get to enjoy  sequences like this but when Vegeta  receives the first punch from broli  and gives us that cheeky grin we know  what's coming and we know how good this  is gonna be the Vegeta fight takes up  about eight minutes of the overall  fights runtime and Yuya Takahashi is in  charge of this section within which we  get to enjoy the shock fall across the  faces of both Broly and para gasp as  Vegeta introduces the Super Saiyan and  Super Saiyan God transformations to the  fight and my god are they handled  beautiful I specifically love the Super  Saiyan transformation as he begins to  glow refusing to let go of broglie's  hand before being enveloped in a massive  golden aura with the camera panning 360  degrees around his stance it's beautiful  this fight however serves one important  purpose primarily to bring Broly  up to speed both figuratively and  literally with the level of combat the  main cast is on through breathtakingly  beautiful tracking shots  Broly slowly gains the upper hand of  vegeta until he finally overpowers the  Saiyan Prince before losing his mind the  fight from here quickly shifts focus to  Goku and Broly again the script clearly  understands that Vegeta is most fun to  watch what he's performing in a dominant  fashion and Goku is most interesting  when he's on the back foot and thus this  transition came at the perfect time  this Goku section is handled primarily  by animator reel on a she who is also  the artist to animated the very first  teaser released for Dragon Ball super  burly and demonstrates some really  experimental animation that I really  enjoyed where the Vegeta fight  established all the regular things we've  come to expect from the series in a  fantastic fashion Goku's fight  introduces new takes on the franchise  through its music selection animation  and lore the music up until this point  of the film has been phenomenal however  much the battle tracks are something you  will either love or hate Sumitomo the  man responsible for the music of the  film felt inspired by the live event  gatherings in latin america during the  final episodes of Dragon Ball super and  so wanted to add chanting and a hype man  for lack of a better term to the tracks  in this section  I enjoyed the experimental nature of it  and if nothing else it's most certainly  memorable from an animation perspective  we got to enjoy a first-person tracking  shot perspective the likes of which I  honestly never seen before in Dragonball  I thought it was a fun idea and worked  well in this long fight to help break up  the monotony on the action but wasn't  majorly impressed and could even see a  lot of people missing this sequence if  you weren't looking for it the fight  itself lasts about 12 minutes in total  for Olli and Goku it has some  interesting new techniques and even has  an explosive Super Saiyan blue  transformation in the middle of things  it does have a few moments of CGI here  and there but with the battle itself  being almost 40 minutes long I'm willing  to forgive the little CGI that was  involved in fact I'd even go as far as  to say that in many other aspects of the  film CGI was used to enhance sequences  beyond what it would have been without  it through backgrounds special effects  and filters amidst all of this action  and explosion para ggest now injured  from being too close reveals to freeze  that that bro Lee must be at his limit  now fortunately Frieza has the perfect  contingency plan  packed with being a magnificent scene  rich in character for Frieza it's also  an almost mirror image of how para Gus  casually killed beats in cold blood  earlier in the film due to the sudden  loss of his father brouilly  overcome with grief begins to transform  during which there's an incredible shot  of Frieza standing front and center  surrounded by flames and destruction all  of his own doing something of interest  also during this cut is that Brawley  blasts his father's body away out of  view never to be seen again in the film  with the situation now more dire than  ever  Vegeta rejoins a fight in what is a  surprisingly effective CGI sequence some  terrific angles backroads choreography  and even angles we wouldn't normally see  in traditional 2d animation overwhelmed  by the hulking enraged Saiyan  both Vegeta and Goku in one of the  funniest moments of the film pond  brewing off on Frieza before making  their way to piccolo somewhere else on  earth using Instant Transmission this  scene is pretty much ripped straight out  of fusion Report and honestly after all  Vegeta has been through in Super with  Goku this scene didn't make sense to me  Vegeta for whatever reason still has a  problem fusing with Goku  understands that it's only 30 minutes  and he understands that he can't do it  any other way  I just honestly can't understand this  hang-up he has he's just fought  alongside Goku in the tournament of  power as well as 30 seconds ago  he's even danced before to save his  friends in battle of gods why is this of  all things an issue for him  simply put because it gives them a  chance to make jokes and to create fake  tension there's really no other reason  I would have preferred if Vegeta showed  the emotional maturity to bring the idea  forth to Goku first that would have been  interesting and a first for the  character needless to say the two of  them agreed to fuse eventually but all  these botched fusion attempts basically  translates to Frieza getting pummeled  for the bones of about an hour before  they eventually arrive as the newly  fused Gogeta makes his Canon debut in  the film now after almost 90 minutes of  the movie having seen some of the most  spectacular animation we've ever seen  from the series one would think that  we've already seen all this film can  show us however nothing could be further  from the truth the remainder of this  fight is packed to bursting with not  only the best animation Dragon Ball has  ever seen but some of the best action  animation I've ever seen period Naruto  shishi that contributes around 1 minute  in 40 seconds of pure movement to the  beginning of this fight and it's  spectacular but seeing as this is an  honest review I do have one small gripe  while everything looks fantastic and  clean the fact that Natasha Sheeta is  held in such high regard within the  company he works for means that he gets  to board his own section which has one  unfortunate side-effect he ends up  repeating angles techniques and  sequences almost exactly the same way  over and over again multiple times  during this sequence I recognize the  composition and ideas from earlier works  and super I'm guessing this isn't  something the regular viewer would even  notice but I did and I thought it worth  mentioning regardless of this small  gripe I still love this spectacular  color of animation from The Incredible  no Toshi cheetah also within this  section is the third and final CGI  sequence but honestly it's the best one  and suits the dimensional shift both  characters undergo its honestly stunning  something also of note once  Cheeta turns Super Saiyan blue rolling  neverland's a hit on him after while  this phenomenal fight is taking place my  last major problem with the film rears  its head she lies desire to save Rolly  by putting her life at risk this leap  from her while I understand it seems a  little premature she already paid Rolly  back for standing up for her after she  stole the remote away from Paris and  while I believed that her and Burleigh  have a fondness for one another that is  believable I find she lies particular  decision here kind of unbelievable this  is a narrative thread that I thought  could have greatly benefited from having  more time exploring it the film did make  a concerted effort to build the  relationship up in three separate scenes  and while I did love their Tarzan and  Jane dynamic they still only knew each  other for a few hours the remaining  moments of the fight are again filled  with some of the most spectacular  animation I've ever seen from Dragonball  full of amazing choreography callbacks  to prior films and character rich  moments the final moments of the battle  are made even more tense with the use of  the Dragon Balls causing the world to be  shrouded in darkness as Gaggia charges  his final kamehameha Broly looks  genuinely scared like he's suddenly come  out of a trance he's beaten and I  sincerely really liked that inclusion  the wish is made to transport Brody back  to home all is back to normal once again  and the fight is over and so now that  everything has been said and done these  are my final thoughts this film really  isn't perfect and as I pointed out has  its shortcomings narrative Lee it isn't  a flawless film and while the first half  does a fantastic job delivering  exposition for first time viewers the  second half really takes off the  training wheels going full force with  its lore and combat so why don't I think  this is the most accessible Dragon Ball  film to date I still would assume that  for most people unfamiliar with the  series prior knowledge of it is required  to get a relatively mediocre level of  enjoyment out of it when all is said and  done however what did I think of it as a  fan of the series I've honestly never  had more fun watching a film to say that  this movie takes you on a ride is an  understatement of the highest order  the fanservice the characters the story  the ridiculous action sequences and set  pieces it's plain as day that the  animators musicians artists writers and  everyone involved we're going  all out with this film it's taken the  best elements from Dragon Ball -  brouilly the legendary Super Saiyan and  fusion reborn to create a brand new  story that is far superior than the sum  of its parts it's not a perfect film and  it has its problems but the  exceptionally great parts of this movie  far outweigh its drawbacks and I highly  recommend anyone who hasn't seen this to  experience it for themselves thanks for  watching  [Music]
 

